 - **Stereotyping the women’s role:** The role of women in India is stereotyped as it is believed that they meant to do household work. The bulk of domestic and care work falls to the woman and most of **this work is unpaid.**  According to the **2019 Oxfam report,** **Mind the Gap – State of Employment in** **India,** Indian women do a cumulative 16.4 billion **hours of unpaid work every day.**  **In 2018, an ILO report found that** 606 million women of working age all over the world declared themselves to be unavailable for employment due to unpaid care work, while only 41 million men were inactive for the same.  They are forced to stay at home and do work that has **neither economic value** **nor social respect. Because of this, they** **cannot go out** and do work that has economic value.

