- It took on a distinct form due to an interaction between what already existed in a society with religiousdiversityandtheideasthatcamefromthe west. It resulted in an equal focus on interreligious and inter-religious domination. Furthermore, it equally opposed the persecution of Dalits and women within Hinduism, the discrimination againstwomenwithinIndianIslamorChristianity, and the viable threats that a majority community might pose to the rights of the minority religious communities.

- The arrival of western modernity led to the fore hitherto neglected and marginalised notions of equality in Indian thought. It sharpened these ideas and assisted us in focusing on equality within the community. It also guided ideas of inter-community equality to replace the notion of hierarchy. Therefore, Indian secularism deals not only with the religious freedom of individuals but also with the religious freedom of minority communities.Withinit,anindividualhastheright to profess the religion of his or her choice. Besides, religious minorities also have the freedom to exist and maintain their own culture and educational institutions.

